# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the unit tests.
#
# These ignore leaks reported in third-party libraries that we link
# against transitively (via Steam, X11, etc.) and have no control over.
# Each pattern matches anywhere in the leak's allocation stack.
#
# Format: `leak:<symbol-or-substring>`. See
# https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/AddressSanitizerLeakSanitizer
# for details.

# D-Bus is initialized indirectly by the Steam runtime / X11 backend
# during process startup. The library leaks ~5KB across a handful of
# allocations inside `dbus_bus_register` and friends. Not our code,
# not actionable from inside the game.
leak:dbus_bus_register
leak:dbus_pending_call_block
leak:_dbus_connection_send_with_reply_and_block
leak:libdbus-1

# `dlopen`-loaded shared objects (Steam, GL drivers) report one-time
# leaks for their internal globals. These are intentional and live for
# the process lifetime.
leak:libGL
leak:libGLX
leak:libsteam_api
